# Normalize every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree,
# on every platform. The `eol=lf` is the part that matters: Git for Windows
# ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config, which would otherwise check
# these files out as CRLF. A stray CR is untidy in Go source but fatal in a
# shell script or Dockerfile once it runs in the Linux container this deploys to.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Insurance against text/binary misdetection on files that are mostly ASCII.
*.db  binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
